<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 74 0 R/E(Our team has grown to nine members, and we aim to inspire more volunteers and coaches to join Rule the Board. A first step in our growth was doubling our impact from four inaugural students to eight this upcoming year, and our goal is to continue supporting as many students as possible. In order to pursue our vision of a nationwide community, we are extending our reach to more areas in which Rule the Board can provide the benefits of chess, bridging the gap between potential and opportunity. )/Pg 14 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

203 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 74 0 R/E(Scholars who have graduated from Rule the Board are forever a part of our community, and part of our dream is to foster a robust network of Rule the Board students, trainers, and alumni. To achieve this, we are working toward hosting our own chess tournament. This tournament will allow scholars to practice in a competitive environment, connect with alumni, and celebrate their achievements.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

